%N A399788 Number of spanning trees in the n-Fibonacci cube graph.
%C A399788 The vertices are length-n binary words with no consecutive 1's, adjacent when they differ in one position. Trees are counted as distinct edge sets, not up to symmetry. For n=0, a(0)=1.
%C A399788 The values for n=1..9 are tabulated in Section 11.3 of Egecioglu, Klavzar, and Mollard.
%H A399788 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A399788/b399788.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..14</a>
%H A399788 O. Egecioglu, S. Klavzar, and M. Mollard, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1142/9789811269158_0011">Further Avenues of Research</a>, in Fibonacci Cubes with Applications and Variations, World Scientific (2023), 259-266; see Section 11.3, 263-265.
%H A399788 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/FibonacciCubeGraph.html">Fibonacci Cube Graph</a>.
%H A399788 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/SpanningTree.html">Spanning Tree</a>.
%F A399788 a(n) >= Fibonacci(n)*a(n-1)*a(n-2), n>=3: split the vertex set into 0 Gamma_(n-1) and 10 Gamma_(n-2), choose a spanning tree in each part and one of the Fibonacci(n) matching edges between the parts. This is a lower bound, not an equality recurrence.
%e A399788 a(2)=1 because the graph is the path 01--00--10.
%e A399788 a(3)=4 because the graph is a 4-cycle on 000,001,101,100 with the leaf 010 attached to 000. A spanning tree keeps the leaf edge and deletes any one of the four cycle edges.
%o A399788 (Python)
%o A399788 from sympy import zeros
%o A399788 def a(n):
%o A399788     vertices = [v for v in range(1 << n) if not v & (v << 1)]
%o A399788     index = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(vertices)}
%o A399788     L = zeros(len(vertices))
%o A399788     for i, v in enumerate(vertices):
%o A399788         for bit in range(n):
%o A399788             j = index.get(v ^ (1 << bit))
%o A399788             if j is not None:
%o A399788                 L[i, i] += 1
%o A399788                 L[i, j] = -1
%o A399788     return L[:-1, :-1].det(method="domain-ge")
%o A399788 print([a(n) for n in range(11)])
%Y A399788 Cf. A000045, A003714, A014417, A245825, A289998, A291935.
